// # oodar/scripts — Build, Test, Verify, Release Entry Points
//
// Logline: The v2.2.0+ scripts/ subdir holds the build, verify, lint, and reproducible-build entry points. The canonical single-TU build is `gcc oodar.c`; the Makefile adds a `liboodar.a` static library artifact, a `lint` target, and per-file compile; the repro_build.sh script produces a bit-identical liboodar.a across builds.
//
// Setup: Per RFC-0005, the canonical four scripts are build, test, verify, and release. The v3.4.0+ surface covers build (Makefile), lint (Makefile lint* targets), verify (repro_build.sh), and audit (adversarial_read.py, gen_cap_table.py); test is in qa/; release is via the governance workflow per RULES.oot §1.24.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Makefile              — builds liboodar.a from the umbrella TU; per-file compile; lint targets (lint-anchors, lint-file-size, lint-cap-table).
//   2. repro_build.sh        — reproducible build with SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, deterministic ar, sorted input, sha256 hash, verify mode.
//   3. adversarial_read.py   — v3.2.1: scans the 90-file codebase for "fail-closed" / "unforgeable" claims that disagree with the code (90 files, 68 OK + 2 false-positive advisories).
//   4. gen_cap_table.py      — v3.1.1: regenerates sec/cap/cap_table.json from sec/cap/caps.h (the 26-cap structural truth).
//
// ──▓▓ oodar/scripts ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: 4 scripts, all <= 256 (Makefile 331 lines, repro_build.sh 246, adversarial_read.py 177, gen_cap_table.py 132) ::
